.TH CIX 1 "CIX 0.1.0" "CIX" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cix \- create a lossless CIX archive
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cix
.RB [ \-1 " ... " \-9 " | " \-\-fast " | " \-\-best ]
.RB [ \-c ]
.RB [ \-f ]
.RB [ \-k ]
.RB [ \-o
.IR file ]
.RI [ file ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cix
compresses one file or standard input into a self-describing CIX archive. With
a named input, the default output name appends
.BR .cix .
Inputs are retained by default. Use
.B \-
as FILE for standard input; use
.B \-c
for standard output. CIX stores one byte stream per invocation; use an
archiver such as tar when preserving a directory tree.
.SH EFFORT AND RESOURCES
.TP
.B \-1 " ... " \-9
Set compression effort. The default is
.BR \-6 .
.TP
.B \-\-fast
Use effort 1 for lower compression latency.
.TP
.B \-\-best
Use effort 9 for the broadest bounded archive search. With no explicit
.BR \-\-memory ,
BEST raises the accounted memory-admission limit to 6 GiB. Decoding, testing,
and listing also start at 6 GiB unless an explicit limit is supplied. This is
not an aggregate-process RSS guarantee. Eligible
whole-file native BEST work can use a 15-minute allowance plus up to 45 minutes
based on input size. Direct external-library calls can add time and are not
preemptible, so this is not a total wall-time limit.
.TP
.BR \-\-memory " " \fISIZE\fR
Set the maximum admitted working memory. SIZE accepts the size syntax accepted
by the command, such as
.BR 512MiB .
FAST and the default profile start at 512 MiB. An explicit value is never
raised automatically.
.TP
.BR \-\-threads " " \fIN\fR
Set the worker limit from 1 through 20. The default is up to four available
CPUs. More than one worker is supported only for native CIXG1/CIXG2 block or
candidate selection.
.TP
.BR \-\-parallelism " " \fIblocks\fR | \fIcandidates\fR
Choose parallel work across ordered blocks or among candidate trials within a
block.
.SH BASIC OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-c
Write the archive to standard output.
.TP
.BR \-o " " \fIFILE\fR
Write the archive to FILE.
.TP
.B \-f
Replace an existing output file.
.TP
.B \-k
Accepted for compatibility. Inputs are retained by default.
.TP
.BR \-h , " " \-\-help
Show command usage.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the version and supported container identifiers.
.SH FORMAT AND EXPERT CONTROLS
These controls constrain the encoder and can exclude otherwise eligible
candidates. They are intended for diagnosis and controlled integration.
.TP
.BR \-\-format " " \fIauto\fR | \fIcixg1\fR | \fIcixg2\fR | \fIcixm6\fR | \fIcixf1\fR
Select or constrain the output container. The default,
.BR auto ,
selects among eligible native containers. CIXM6 and CIXF1 are encoding-only
formats and cannot be combined with route selection, external candidates, or
portfolio selection. CIXF1 requires a named input so its basename can be
stored. An explicit non-auto format forces a compatible whole-container wire
and excludes unrelated automatic carriers.
.TP
.BR \-\-route " " \fIauto\fR | \fIraw\fR | \fIruns\fR | \fIcomposition\fR | \fIlz\fR | \fIpredictor\fR | \fIbwt\fR | \fIstride\fR | \fIphrases\fR | \fIppm\fR | \fImixture\fR | \fIdeflate\fR
Constrain the native route. Some routes need more memory: LZ and mixture need
at least 16 MiB, and PPM needs at least 64 MiB.
.TP
.BR \-\-backend " " \fINAME\fR
Constrain the nested substream backend. Supported names are
.BR cix ,
.BR raw ,
.BR runs ,
.BR ppm ,
.BR mixture ,
.BR deflate ,
.BR hybrid ,
.BR range ,
.BR count-range ,
.BR context-range-o1-b4 ,
.BR context-range-o1-b8 ,
.BR context-range-o2-b8 ,
and
.BR huffman .
Some versioned substream coders require CIXG2 or automatic format selection.
This is native-container tuning: without an explicit non-auto
.BR --format ,
independent automatic candidates remain eligible and do not claim to use the
selected nested backend.
.TP
.BR \-\-block-size " " \fISIZE\fR
Set the maximum uncompressed block size. CIXG1 frames are limited to 65536
bytes; larger requests are reduced to that limit with a diagnostic. The legacy
.B \-\-block
form accepts a byte count. This is native-container tuning; it restricts native
block candidates without forcing the automatic search to one container wire.
.TP
.BR \-\-history " " \fISIZE\fR
Request retained model history. The current native routes do not support a
nonzero value and reject it.
.TP
.B \-\-independent-blocks
Request model reset boundaries. It conflicts with retained history and is not
available for CIXM6/CIXF1 or external/portfolio encoding.
.TP
.B \-\-stream
Require streaming operation. Streaming uses bounded framed candidates; it
cannot be used with whole-input external or portfolio selection.
.TP
.BR \-\-flush-interval " " \fIDURATION\fR
Flush framed partial blocks after an idle interval while encoding. It is not a
decoding option. For non-seekable input, it requires Unix poll support.
.TP
.BR \-\-profile " " \fIfast\fR | \fIdefault\fR | \fIsize\fR
Choose an external profile or map a native auto/CIXG1/CIXG2 encode to effort
1, 6, or 9. It cannot be combined with a numeric effort option.
.TP
.BR \-\-portfolio " " \fIfast\fR | \fIdefault\fR | \fIsize\fR
Use bounded whole-input CIXB1 portfolio selection, comparing eligible native
and direct external candidates before choosing one completed archive. This is
whole-input portfolio selection, not per-symbol predictive mixing. It requires
a named bounded input and conflicts with streaming, route, external, and
profile controls.
.TP
.BR \-\-external " " \fICODEC\fR
Explicitly wrap a direct external codec in CIXB1. It is an encoding-only,
named-input operation and conflicts with streaming and route selection.
.TP
.B \-\-explain
Report candidate costs and decisions.
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
Report aggregate search statistics and resource exclusions.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 indicates success. A nonzero status indicates invalid arguments, I/O failure,
resource admission failure, interruption, or compression failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR uncix (1),
.BR cixcat (1)
